course: dictionary
lesson: 9407
title: Squander: wasting something precious
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To squander something is to waste it foolishly. You can squander money, time or a chance. The word is about being careless with something valuable, so you do not get the good result you could have had.
explain: Read this from The Wind in the Willows: «you've gone on squandering the money your father left you». The clues are money, your father left you, and furious driving and smashes. The Badger is cross because someone is spending careless and foolish. Squander must mean waste.
explain: Squander can also be about a talent or a chance. A team that is ahead in a match and then loses has squandered its lead. Ask yourself: is something valuable being used badly? If yes, squander is probably the right word.
fact: To squander something means to waste it foolishly.
fact: You can squander money, time or a chance.
fact: «Squander» is often used as a warning in stories, when a character spends or wastes what they should keep.
fact: A team that loses after leading has squandered its lead.
fact: Squander is a verb: squander, squanders, squandered, squandering.
exercise: «you've gone on squandering the money your father left you» What does squandering mean here? | Counting and sorting into piles | Giving it back to the bank | Saving carefully for later | *Wasting foolishly
exercise: The team was three goals ahead, then lost the match. They ___ their lead. | measured | *squandered | drew | guarded
exercise: Which is the best example of squandering money? | Counting coins at the bank | *Buying sweets every day until the pocket money is gone | Lending a pencil to a friend | Saving coins in a jar for a new bike
test: Which word is closest in meaning to squander? | *Waste | Protect | Admire | Gather
test: «She squandered her talent by never practising.» What does this mean? | She shared her talent with others | *She did not use her talent well | She lost her talent in the park | She practised every day and got better
exam: Which sentence shows someone squandering a chance? | He wrote the word chance in his book | He saved the chance in a box | He grabbed the chance and practised every day | *He let the chance slip by while he played games
